Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS  
  – "sample_path" : filter to Java files with ILIKE '%.java'  
  – "content" : full file text we need to split into lines and search for import statements  
  – "sample_repo_name" : keep repo context, optional grouping  
• GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES  
  – "path" / "id" : alternate way to locate Java files or join to contents (not strictly needed but useful)  

Typical conditions that will get used  
• "sample_path" ILIKE '%.java' – restrict to Java source  
• LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE("content", '\n') – break each file into individual lines  
• f.value ILIKE 'import %' – retain only import‑statement lines  
• REGEXP_SUBSTR / REGEXP_REPLACE – pull out just the package portion, dropping the class name  
• GROUP BY the extracted package, COUNT(*) and ORDER BY that count DESC  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows except the last one that naturally returns the top‑10 packages).  
All column names are double‑quoted as required.

```sql
-- 1) Quick look at a few Java files that exist in the sample contents table
SELECT 
  "sample_repo_name",
  "sample_path"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE "sample_path" ILIKE '%.java'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Count how many Java source files each repo contributes to the sample
SELECT
  "sample_repo_name",
  COUNT(*) AS "java_file_count"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE "sample_path" ILIKE '%.java'
GROUP BY "sample_repo_name"
ORDER BY "java_file_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Peek at the raw text of some Java files
SELECT
  "sample_repo_name",
  "sample_path",
  "content"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE "sample_path" ILIKE '%.java'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Split one random Java file into lines so we can inspect individual statements
SELECT
  f.value AS "line_text"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') f
WHERE c."sample_path" ILIKE '%.java'
  AND c."sample_repo_name" IS NOT NULL   -- arbitrary filter so we only sample one / few
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Show only those lines that look like import statements
SELECT
  f.value AS "import_line"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') f
WHERE c."sample_path" ILIKE '%.java'
  AND f.value ILIKE 'import %'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Extract the fully‑qualified symbol from each import line
SELECT
  REGEXP_SUBSTR(f.value, 'import\\s+(?:static\\s+)?([A-Za-z0-9_\\.]+)', 1, 1, 'e', 1) AS "full_symbol"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') f
WHERE c."sample_path" ILIKE '%.java'
  AND f.value ILIKE 'import %'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Trim the class‑name suffix so we are left with just the package portion
SELECT
  REGEXP_REPLACE(
        REGEXP_SUBSTR(f.value, 'import\\s+(?:static\\s+)?([A-Za-z0-9_\\.]+)', 1, 1, 'e', 1),
        '\\.[^\\.]+$',
        ''
  ) AS "package_name"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') f
WHERE c."sample_path" ILIKE '%.java'
  AND f.value ILIKE 'import %'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Count how often each package name appears (preview top‑20)
SELECT
  REGEXP_REPLACE(
        REGEXP_SUBSTR(f.value, 'import\\s+(?:static\\s+)?([A-Za-z0-9_\\.]+)', 1, 1, 'e', 1),
        '\\.[^\\.]+$',
        ''
  ) AS "package_name",
  COUNT(*) AS "occurrences"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') f
WHERE c."sample_path" ILIKE '%.java'
  AND f.value ILIKE 'import %'
GROUP BY "package_name"
ORDER BY "occurrences" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Same as #8 but restricted to non‑empty, well‑formed packages only
SELECT
  REGEXP_REPLACE(
        REGEXP_SUBSTR(f.value, 'import\\s+(?:static\\s+)?([A-Za-z0-9_\\.]+)', 1, 1, 'e', 1),
        '\\.[^\\.]+$',
        ''
  ) AS "package_name",
  COUNT(*) AS "occurrences"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') f
WHERE c."sample_path" ILIKE '%.java'
  AND f.value ILIKE 'import %'
  AND REGEXP_SUBSTR(f.value, 'import\\s+(?:static\\s+)?([A-Za-z0-9_\\.]+)', 1, 1, 'e', 1) IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY "package_name"
ORDER BY "occurrences" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Final query: top‑10 most frequently imported Java packages across all sampled repos
SELECT
  REGEXP_REPLACE(
        REGEXP_SUBSTR(f.value, 'import\\s+(?:static\\s+)?([A-Za-z0-9_\\.]+)', 1, 1, 'e', 1),
        '\\.[^\\.]+$',
        ''
  ) AS "package_name",
  COUNT(*) AS "occurrences"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(c."content", '\n') f
WHERE c."sample_path" ILIKE '%.java'
  AND f.value ILIKE 'import %'
  AND REGEXP_SUBSTR(f.value, 'import\\s+(?:static\\s+)?([A-Za-z0-9_\\.]+)', 1, 1, 'e', 1) IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY "package_name"
ORDER BY "occurrences" DESC
LIMIT 10;
```

These ten queries progress from basic inspection of Java files through to the full aggregation that returns the ten most frequently imported package names.
